# Frontend architecture

Stack: React + TypeScript + Vite + Ant Design.

- Use AntD for buttons, forms, layout, tables, modals, etc. Do not recreate those primitives.
- `components/ui/` is only NutriVision-specific widgets built on AntD.
- `components/layout/` holds `AppLayout` and `PublicLayout`.
- `pages/` = screens. `services/{Domain}Service/` = API clients aligned with `backend/services/{domain}/`.
- `AppRoutes/` = React Router + `PrivateRoute`.
- No `features/`, `container/`, `atoms/`, `molecules/`, `organisms/`.
- No extra global state; auth uses `useAuth` + session JWT.
- PascalCase for pages/services/components; camelCase for hooks/utils.

```text
AuthService/AuthService.ts  →  backend/services/auth/   ✅
pages/Login/LoginPage.tsx                               ✅
components/ui/Button.tsx                                ❌
```
